items.Nakasar_Fractal_Astrolabe_Ring.name = Astrolabe Ring
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Astrolabe_Ring.description = Armillary ring of the Astrolabe.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Harmony_Tile.name = Attunement Tile
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Harmony_Tile.description = Players standing on the circle form the group (5 at most).
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Gate_Veil.name = Asura Gate Veil
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Gate_Veil.description = Walk through it: return home.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Gate_Heart.name = Asura Gate Heart
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Gate_Heart.description = The swirl of the Mists at the heart of the gate. Walk through it: return home.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Asura_Console.name = Asura Console
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Asura_Console.description = Its holograms follow the fractals the Observatory watches over.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Light_Spring.name = Light Spring
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Light_Spring.description = A fall of Mists light pours into the pool.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Trial_Panel.name = Training Golem Console
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Trial_Panel.description = Use: the golem replays the fractal attacks on you.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Mists_Portal.name = Mists Portal
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Mists_Portal.description = An arch to place at home, always open: walking through leads to the Fractal Observatory, no Mists Fragment needed. Can be broken and picked up again.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Exit_Stone.name = Return Stone
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Exit_Stone.description = Use: back to the Observatory.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Infusion_Altar.name = Infusion Altar
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Infusion_Altar.description = Use: your 12 infusion slots. Each infusion placed adds its agony resistance, wherever you are; removing it takes it away.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Mist_Forge.name = Mist Crucible
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Mist_Forge.description = Fuses two identical infusions into the next one, and remakes a Mist Fragment from shards.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Reward_Chest.name = Fractal Reward Chest
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Reward_Chest.description = Use: your reward (one per group member). Completing a fractal at your highest level unlocks the next one.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Archivist_Counter.name = Archivist's Counter
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Archivist_Counter.description = Use: trade Mist Shards for infusions, fragments and seasonal cosmetics.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Daily_Board.name = Daily Fractals Board
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Daily_Board.description = Use: today's three daily fractals. Completing one gives, the first time each day, an extra Daily Fractal Chest.
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Registry.name = Fractal Registry
items.Nakasar_Fractal_Registry.description = Welcome to the Observatory, traveller of the Mists.\n\n1. Take a fractal core and a level tuning fork from the two dispensers at the circle's entrance.\n2. Place them in the selection console on the Astrolabe: the circle attunes to that fractal.\n3. Step onto the attunement circle: players standing on it form the group, five at most. The first to arrive in the Observatory leads it.\n4. The leader uses a circle resonator: the whole circle leaves.\n\nSeason 1: Cliffside, Uncategorized, Volcanic, Solid Ocean, Swampland, Snowblind.\nSeason 2: Silent Surf, Siren's Reef.\nThe training golem, to the west, lets you test your hits, your agony resistance and see the fractal attacks.\nTo the east, the Archivist trades Mist Shards and Dessa's Alchemist sells Mist potions; the Infusion Altar holds your agony resistance and the Mist Crucible fuses infusions.\nEach fractal completed at your highest level unlocks the next; the leader can only pick a level they have unlocked.\n\nFallback command: /fractale (niveau, groupe, lancer, quitter, infos).
